### 4. Git Push Commands
The repo is committed locally on the `main` branch. To push to GitHub, run:

```bash
cd my_website

# Add the remote (replace with your actual repo URL)
git remote add origin https://github.com/<username>/<repo-name>.git

# Push to main branch
git push -u origin main

# Run existing GitHub workflows (they trigger on push to main)
# The deploy workflow will automatically run on push.
# To manually trigger via CLI:
gh workflow run deploy.yml --ref main
```

